Upstream-Status: Pending

Origin: Fedora (Tomasz Torcz <ttorcz@fedoraproject.org>)
Bug-Report: https://sourceforge.net/p/nicstat/bugs/1/
Bug-Fedora: https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2145035

Fix integer overflow on 10G+ interfaces and read 32-bit speed via
ethtool_cmd_speed() for 100G+ interfaces.
Exit: Drop when upstream nicstat releases > 1.95 with ethtool_cmd_speed().

--- a/nicstat.c
+++ b/nicstat.c
@@ -1609,7 +1609,7 @@ get_speed_duplex(nicdata_t *nicp)
 		get_speed_duplex(nicp);
 		return;
 	}
-	nicp->speed = edata.speed * 1000000;
+	nicp->speed = (uint64_t) ethtool_cmd_speed(&edata) * 1000000;
 	nicp->duplex = edata.duplex;
 }
 #endif /* OS_LINUX */
